    "q-182582": {
      "dom_id": "step-q182582",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,(A∧¬B)⇔(A∨B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-4}} |",
      "worked_solution": "According to the definition of the biconditional, \n\n- $P⇔Q$ is true if $P⇒Q$ **and** $Q⇒P.$ Otherwise, it is false.\n\n- In other words, $P⇔Q$ is true if $P$ and $Q$ have the same truth values. Otherwise, it is false.\n\nFirst, we add columns for $¬B,$ $A∧¬B,$ and $A∨B:$\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬B\\,$ | $\\,A∧¬B\\,$ | $\\,A∨B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nFinally, we add a column for $(A∧¬B)⇔(A∨B).$ \n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬B\\,$ | $\\,A∧¬B\\,$ | $\\,A∨B\\,$ | $\\,(A∧¬B)⇔(A∨B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
