    "q-107160": {
      "dom_id": "step-q107160",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "$$\nX⇔(Y∧X)≡\\bbox[3pt,white,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAAAAAAA}}∧[(Y∧X)⇒X]\n$$\n\nWhat expression should be inserted into the blank space above to give logically equivalent statements?",
      "worked_solution": "According to the definition of the biconditional, \n\n- $A⇔B$ is true if $A⇒B$ **and** $B⇒A.$ Otherwise, it is false.\n\n- In other words, $A⇔B$ is true if $A$ and $B$ have the same truth values. Otherwise, it is false.\n\nSo, in this case, we have\n\n$$\nX⇔(Y∧X)≡[\\,X⇒(Y∧X)]∧[(Y∧X)⇒X].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing part is $X⇒(Y∧X).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
