    "q-1471": {
      "dom_id": "step-q1471",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "$P⇔Q≡$",
      "worked_solution": "According to the definition of the biconditional, \n\n- $A⇔B$ is true if $A⇒B$ **and** $B⇒A.$ Otherwise, it is false.\n\n- In other words, $A⇔B$ is true if $A$ and $B$ have the same truth values. Otherwise, it is false.\n\nSo in this case, we have\n\n$$\nP⇔Q≡(P⇒Q)∧(Q⇒P).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
