    "q-182522": {
      "dom_id": "step-q182522",
      "name": "Question 20",
      "problem": "$¬(B⇔A)≡$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we use the definition of the biconditional statement to write the equivalence as a conjunction of implications: \n\n$$\n¬(B⇔A)≡¬[(B⇒A)∧(A⇒B)]\n$$\n\nNow, we represent all the implications using disjunctions and negations:\n\n$$\n¬[(B⇒A)∧(A⇒B)]≡¬[(¬B∨A)∧(¬A∨B)]\n$$\n\nNext, we use De Morgan's laws:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬[(¬B∨A)∧(¬A∨B)] & ≡¬(¬B∨A)∨¬(¬A∨B) \\\\  & ≡(¬¬B∧¬A)∨(¬¬A∧¬B)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the double negations and write down symbols in alphabetic order inside the parentheses using commutative laws:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(¬¬B∧¬A)∨(¬¬A∧¬B) & ≡(B∧¬A)∨(A∧¬B) \\\\  & ≡(¬A∧B)∨(A∧¬B)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
